":0.04,"dividend_yield":0.34,"payout_ratio":0.0774,"five_yr_avg_div_yield":6.78,"revenue":8880397484032.0,"revenue_per_share":20616.72,"revenue_growth":0.305,"ebitda":2480229056512.0,"ebitda_margins":0.27929002,"gross_margins":0.75732005,"operating_margins":0.12482,"profit_margins":0.03925,"net_income":348575989760.0,"total_cash":1069764968448.0,"total_cash_per_share":2483.565,"total_debt":5891171024896.0,"debt_to_equity":71.681,"current_ratio":0.581,"free_cashflow":939884347392.0,"return_on_equity":0.052270003,"enterprise_value":4951355949056.0,"enterprise_to_ebitda":1.996,"enterprise_to_revenue":0.558,"earnings_growth":4.391,"shares_outstanding":125611604.0,"float_shares":32529304.0,"held_pct_insiders":0.00101,"held_pct_institutions":0.12923999,"beta":0.374,"fifty_two_week_high":16.34,"fifty_two_week_low":6.43,"fifty_day_average":12.8238,"two_hundred_day_avg":11.42595,"target_high_price":19.0,"target_low_price":9.2,"target_mean_price":15.4998,"recommendation":"buy","num_analyst_opinions":5,"all_time_high":46.75,"all_time_low":0.6,"long_business_summary":"Telecom Argentina S.A., together with its subsidiaries, provides telecommunications services in Argentina, Paraguay, Uruguay, Chile and the United States. The company offers mobile telecommunications services, including voice communications, high-speed mobile internet content and applications download, online streaming, and other services; and sells mobile communication devices, such as handsets, modems, MiFi and wingles, and smartwatches. It also offers internet connectivity products, including virtual private network services, traditional internet protocol links, and other products; and programming and other cable television services. In addition, the company provides telephone services, including local, domestic, and international long-distance telephone services, as well as public telephone services; and other related supplementary services, such as call waiting, call forwarding, conference calls, caller ID, voice mail, itemized billing, and maintenance services. Further, it offers infrastructure, interconnection, datacenter, internet, value added, and international long-distance services; and data services, including data transmission, virtual private networks, symmetric internet access, national and international signal transport, and videoconferencing services; Personal Pay, a digital wallet service. The company also offers broadcasting, cable television, financial, cybersecurity, ICT services and audiovisual communication, content platform and related services; security solutions and services; closed-circuit and community closed-circuit television, as well as investment and consulting services. The company was formerly known as Cablevisi\u00f3n S.A. and changed its name to Telecom Argentina S.A. in January 2018. Telecom Argentina S.A. was founded in 1979 and is based in Buenos Aires, Argentina."}}